  "body": "Consider the following meta viewport tag:\r\n```html\r\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width;\">\r\n```\r\n\r\nBoth chrome and safari ignore this tag due to the semicolon. However, firefox treats the semicolon the same as a separator just like comma...\r\n\r\nIs this specified anywhere? Should we have firefox follow the chrome/safari behavior?\r\n\r\nI found this in [this chrome bug](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=512351), and the semicolon behavior appears to have been added in [this patch](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/83b6b8dffe760131d099a8daba1a84319e699178%5E%21/). ",
